{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/retrypolicy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" retries a flush whose save failed."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RetryPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Retrying matters because the buffers are cleared at flush time: without it a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"failed save only ever reaches disk if the user happens to touch the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity again, which is silent data loss. Retrying "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"forever","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" matters just as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"much in the other direction — a write that can never succeed (disk full, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"model the container can’t encode, a schema mismatch) must not keep the stack"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy indefinitely. So attempts are bounded, and running out is an event the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app can see rather than a silence."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/RetryPolicy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"externalID":"s:6Swidux11RetryPolicyV","title":"RetryPolicy","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RetryPolic